; A robot in a maze.  Ours, after RN-2008-003's figure (sections 4 and 10): a 4 by 4 grid,
; C1, D1, D2 and D3 blocked, the robot from A1 to D4, a visited square blocked behind it.
start-world maze.
create Square col row blocked.
create Robot position.
make Square A1 1 1 yes. make Square B1 2 1 no. make Square C1 3 1 yes. make Square D1 4 1 yes.
make Square A2 1 2 no.  make Square B2 2 2 no. make Square C2 3 2 no.  make Square D2 4 2 yes.
make Square A3 1 3 no.  make Square B3 2 3 no. make Square C3 3 3 no.  make Square D3 4 3 yes.
make Square A4 1 4 no.  make Square B4 2 4 no. make Square C4 3 4 no.  make Square D4 4 4 no.
make Robot R A1.
rel-qualify Square:S1 adjacent Square:S2 if
  (S1 col = S2 col and (S1 row = S2 row + 1 or S1 row + 1 = S2 row)) or
  (S1 row = S2 row and (S1 col = S2 col + 1 or S1 col + 1 = S2 col)).
action Robot move Square consequence its position = Square and Square blocked = yes.
rule Robot move is Square blocked = no.
rule Robot move is Square adjacent its position.
goal Robot reach try its position = D4.
; how far from D4, in moves on an open grid
heuristic Robot reach 1 minimize (4 - its position col) + (4 - its position row).
